e(4,'pair-counts','Pair labels and counts','Use `zip()` to pair labels with counts and print each pair.','Line 1: labels. Line 2: integer counts. The lists have equal length; both may be empty.','One `<label>: <count>` line per pair, in input order.','labels = input().split()\ncounts = [int(value) for value in input().split()]\nfor label, count in zip(labels, counts):\n    print(f"{label}: {count}")',[tc(['A B','3 0'],'A: 3\nB: 0'),tc(['',''],''),tc(['C A B','8 2 5'],'C: 8\nA: 2\nB: 5')],hint='`zip(labels, counts)` yields matching pairs.')
