e(4,'sampling-tool','A command-line sampling tool','Complete the argument parser and use `random.Random(seed).randint(1, 6)` count times. Print the label and generated integers. A seed makes the result repeatable.','Command-line arguments `--label` (text), `--seed` (non-negative integer), `--count` (integer 1–10). No stdin.','`<label>: <numbers joined by spaces>`.','import argparse\nimport random\nparser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\nparser.add_argument("--label", required=True)\nparser.add_argument("--seed", type=int, required=True)\nparser.add_argument("--count", type=int, required=True)\nargs = parser.parse_args()\nrng = random.Random(args.seed)\nvalues = [rng.randint(1, 6) for _ in range(args.count)]\nprint(args.label + ": " + " ".join(map(str, values)))',sampling,hint='Create the generator once, before the loop. Do not reset its seed for every value.',starter='import argparse\nimport random\nparser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\nparser.add_argument("--label", required=True)\nparser.add_argument("--seed", type=int, required=True)\nparser.add_argument("--count", type=int, required=True)\nargs = parser.parse_args()\n# Create the generator, generate values, and print\n',difficulty='Harder')
