e(5,'organise-copies','Organise files and compare copies','Create `selected` and copy only the input directory\'s top-level `.txt` files there with `shutil.copyfile()`. Print copied basenames alphabetically. Then compare all copied files using `filecmp.cmp(..., shallow=False)`.','One supplied directory path.','Copied basenames, one per line, followed by `copies identical: yes` when every copy matches (also when no files match). Create exactly those copies under `selected`.','import glob\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport filecmp\ndirectory = input()\nos.mkdir("selected")\nidentical = True\nfor source in sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(directory, "*.txt"))):\n    if not os.path.isfile(source):\n        continue\n    name = os.path.basename(source)\n    target = os.path.join("selected", name)\n    shutil.copyfile(source, target)\n    identical = identical and filecmp.cmp(source, target, shallow=False)\n    print(name)\nprint("copies identical: " + ("yes" if identical else "no"))',[tc(['python-course/copy-a'],'A.txt\nsample B.txt\ncopies identical: yes',fixtures=['python-course/copy-a'],outputFiles=['selected','selected/A.txt','selected/sample B.txt']),tc(['python-course/copy-b'],'C.txt\ncopies identical: yes',fixtures=['python-course/copy-b'],outputFiles=['selected','selected/C.txt']),tc(['python-course/copy-c'],'copies identical: yes',fixtures=['python-course/copy-c'],outputFiles=['selected'])],hint='The supplied imports and directory creation are scaffolding; complete the copy loop.',starter='import glob\nimport os\nimport shutil\nimport filecmp\ndirectory = input()\nos.mkdir("selected")\n# Copy, compare and list the matching files\n',difficulty='Medium',file_example='selected/A.txt: alpha\nselected/sample B.txt: beta')
