e(9,'inspect-array','Inspect a numerical array','Read six integers and form a NumPy array of shape (2, 3) using dtype `np.int64`. Print its shape, number of dimensions, size and the element at row 1, column 2 (zero-based).','One line containing exactly six integers. Fill the array in row order.','Four lines: `shape: (2, 3)`, `dimensions: 2`, `size: 6`, `selected: <element>`.','import numpy as np\narray = np.array([int(value) for value in input().split()], dtype=np.int64).reshape(2, 3)\nprint(f"shape: {array.shape}")\nprint(f"dimensions: {array.ndim}")\nprint(f"size: {array.size}")\nprint(f"selected: {array[1, 2]}")',[tc(['1 2 3 4 5 6'],'shape: (2, 3)\ndimensions: 2\nsize: 6\nselected: 6'),tc(['0 -1 2 3 4 -5'],'shape: (2, 3)\ndimensions: 2\nsize: 6\nselected: -5'),tc(['9 8 7 6 5 0'],'shape: (2, 3)\ndimensions: 2\nsize: 6\nselected: 0')],hint='NumPy is installed. Use `.reshape(2, 3)` after creating the array.',starter='import numpy as np\nvalues = [int(value) for value in input().split()]\n# Create the array and print its properties\n')
