e(10,'inspect-image','Inspect an image','Open the supplied PNG with Pillow and print its width, height and colour mode.','One PNG filename.','`width: <n>`, `height: <n>`, `mode: <mode>` on separate lines.','from PIL import Image\nwith Image.open(input()) as image:\n    print(f"width: {image.width}")\n    print(f"height: {image.height}")\n    print(f"mode: {image.mode}")',[tc([img_a],'width: 6\nheight: 4\nmode: RGB',fixtures=[img_a]),tc([img_b],'width: 4\nheight: 6\nmode: RGB',fixtures=[img_b]),tc([img_g],'width: 5\nheight: 3\nmode: L',fixtures=[img_g])],hint='Use `Image.open()`. RGB stores colour channels; L is grayscale. Do not call `Image.show()`.',starter='from PIL import Image\nfilename = input()\n# Open the image and print its properties\n')
