e(10,'grayscale','Convert to grayscale','Load an RGB PNG with skimage.io.imread and convert it using skimage.color.rgb2gray. Print the shape and intensities at row/column (0,0) and (1,1).','One RGB PNG filename, at least 2 × 2 pixels.','`shape: (<height>, <width>)`, `pixel(0,0): <four decimals>`, `pixel(1,1): <four decimals>`. Intensities range from 0 to 1.','from skimage import io, color\ngray = color.rgb2gray(io.imread(input()))\nprint(f"shape: {gray.shape}")\nprint(f"pixel(0,0): {gray[0, 0]:.4f}")\nprint(f"pixel(1,1): {gray[1, 1]:.4f}")',gray_tests,hint='This is a weighted conversion, not a simple average. Images are indexed as [row, column].',difficulty='Medium')
